# Repo-wide line-ending policy: normalize text to LF on checkin, check out
# as LF everywhere (including Windows, regardless of a machine's local
# core.autocrlf). This is what actually fixes cross-machine reproducibility
# for tidy-agent's frozen eval fixtures (see below) instead of only papering
# over it for their specific paths.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.ipynb text eol=lf

# Explicit binary markers: never let `text=auto`'s content heuristic or a
# renormalize touch these, regardless of what any individual file's bytes
# look like. This matters most for tidy-agent's synthetic eval fixtures,
# where a file with e.g. a .jpg/.zip extension is often a tiny, NUL-free
# text stub standing in for that format (used to test extension-based
# classification) rather than real binary content -- content-based
# auto-detection alone would not protect those.
*.png binary
*.pt binary
*.safetensors binary
*.eml binary
*.7z binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.zip binary

# tidy-agent's frozen eval fixtures: their SHA-256 is verified byte-for-byte
# against committed fixture_manifest.json files (see
# projects/tidy-agent/evals/freeze_datasets.py and
# _verify_dataset_manifest() in
# projects/tidy-agent/evals/run_structured_abcd.py). Without a pinned
# eol, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true (the GitHub Actions
# windows-latest default) silently rewrites LF to CRLF in these files, which
# breaks that hash check even though nothing "changed". The blanket
# `* text=auto eol=lf` above already covers this; these lines are kept as
# explicit, self-documenting pins for the paths that are actually
# hash-verified, so their normalization doesn't depend on staying in sync
# with unrelated repo-wide policy changes above.
projects/tidy-agent/evals/**/fixture/** text eol=lf
projects/tidy-agent/evals/**/expected.yaml text eol=lf
projects/tidy-agent/evals/holdout_v4/ground_truth.json text eol=lf

# Exceptions: frozen fixtures whose blob deliberately contains raw binary
# content (including embedded CR/LF bytes as part of that content, not as
# line endings). Keep them binary so normalization never rewrites their
# frozen bytes.
projects/tidy-agent/evals/fixture/geraetedump -text
projects/tidy-agent/evals/holdout/fixture/camera_blob -text
